      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Difference Between Plant Cell and Animal Cell"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Match the discoveries: Robert Hooke (Cell, 1665), Anton van Leeuwenhoek (Live Cell, 1674), and Robert Brown (Nucleus, 1831).",
        "Mitochondria and Chloroplasts are semi-autonomous organelles containing their own circular DNA and 70S ribosomes.",
        "Plant cell walls consist of cellulose, fungal cell walls consist of chitin, and bacterial cell walls consist of peptidoglycan.",
        "Ribosomes are non-membrane-bound organelles present in both prokaryotic (70S) and eukaryotic (80S) cells."
      ],
      "id": "dop9ec3"
    },
